IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bdm-registration`
IMPORT `bdm-cause-of-death`

-- Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA), ss 2, 12-19, 22, Part 6 and Part 7 -- worked cases. Conformed to the
-- writing-l4-rules skill on 14 October 2026, and to section 5 of docs/ENCODING-GUIDE.md (the stable l4, 1.6.98) on 22 October 2026.
--
-- Every assertion and every trace is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Expected results were written by hand from the text. A DEONTIC cannot be asserted, so the boolean tests are #ASSERTed and the
-- duties are #TRACEd (the phrasebook, entry 5.11). Each #TRACE has an "-- expect:" line above it. A question the encoding does not
-- cover is asserted to answer `not covered`, with the reason it names. Clocks: DAYS for every trace except s 44's, which is in
-- HOURS (see the two modules' headers). Edit this file directly; the generator that first laid out its fixtures is retired.

§ `s 2 -- commencement (daniel d001, chloe c001)`

#ASSERT `the operation of the Act on` (YMD 1996 4 18) EQUALS `the Act was not yet in operation`
#ASSERT `the operation of the Act on` (YMD 2003 4 2) EQUALS `the Act was in operation`
#ASSERT `the operation of the Act on` (YMD 1999 4 14) EQUALS `the Act was in operation`

§ `s 12 -- who notifies a birth, and by when (chloe c062: a public hospital is assumed for KEMH)`

`a birth in a public hospital` MEANS Birth WITH
    `date of the birth` IS YMD 2030 9 5
    `in the State` IS TRUE
    `hospital involved` IS `a public hospital`
    `a stillbirth` IS FALSE
    `a doctor or midwife in attendance` IS TRUE
    `registration ordered by a State court` IS FALSE
    `in an aircraft or on a vessel on the way to the State` IS FALSE
    `outside the Commonwealth, the child to become a resident of the State` IS FALSE
    `registered under a corresponding law` IS FALSE
    `a foundling` IS FALSE
    `a neonatal death` IS FALSE

