-- 5 October 2030 is day 30, the last day of the month: in time. 6 October is day 31: late.
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 12(2) -- the responsible person must give the Registrar notice of the birth within one month` `a birth in a public hospital` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the chief executive of the health service provider` DOES `give the Registrar notice of the birth` AT 30

-- expect: BREACH "s 12(2): the responsible person did not give the Registrar notice of the birth within one month after the birth"
#TRACE `s 12(2) -- the responsible person must give the Registrar notice of the birth within one month` `a birth in a public hospital` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the chief executive of the health service provider` DOES `give the Registrar notice of the birth` AT 31

-- s 12(3): another person's notice takes away the OFFENCE (asserted above), not the DUTY, which the responsible person still
-- did not perform. The trace reports the breach; the offence predicate says there is no offence.
-- expect: BREACH "s 12(2): the responsible person did not give the Registrar notice of the birth within one month after the birth"
#TRACE `s 12(2) -- the responsible person must give the Registrar notice of the birth within one month` `a birth in a public hospital` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `another person` DOES `give the Registrar notice of the birth` AT 10
    (WAITUNTIL 31)

-- expect: residual
#TRACE `s 12(2) -- the responsible person must give the Registrar notice of the birth within one month` `a home birth with a midwife` AT 0 WITH
    -- no events

-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 12(2) -- the responsible person must give the Registrar notice of the birth within one month` `a home birth with no doctor or midwife` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `any person in attendance at the birth` DOES `give the Registrar notice of the birth` AT 3

-- expect: FULFILLED
