§ `s 44 -- the doctor's certificate (chloe c086: not reportable to a coroner). This section's clock is HOURS.`

`a certificate at 50 hours` MEANS `The doctor's certificate` WITH
    `hours after the death it was given` IS 50
    `given by another doctor` IS FALSE
    `the doctor had reasonable cause for not being able to comply` IS FALSE

`a certificate at 48 hours` MEANS `The doctor's certificate` WITH
    `hours after the death it was given` IS 48
    `given by another doctor` IS FALSE
    `the doctor had reasonable cause for not being able to comply` IS FALSE

`a certificate at 50 hours, with reasonable cause` MEANS `The doctor's certificate` WITH
    `hours after the death it was given` IS 50
    `given by another doctor` IS FALSE
    `the doctor had reasonable cause for not being able to comply` IS TRUE

`a death in the State on 1 January 1999` MEANS Death WITH
    `date of the death` IS YMD 1999 1 1
    `in the State` IS TRUE
    `registration ordered by a State court or coroner` IS FALSE
    `the death of a stillborn child` IS FALSE
    `the remains placed for medical education or research` IS FALSE
    `reportable to a coroner under section 17(3) of the Coroners Act 1996` IS FALSE
    `a suspected death established at an inquest` IS FALSE
    `a coronial investigation into the cause incomplete` IS FALSE
    `date of the disposal` IS NOTHING

